meta {
  name: Update User Details
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/users/{{invitedUserId}}/details
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{ownerAccessToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

script:pre-request {
  // Two digits, sent unpadded to show it is stored zero-padded. 60–98 stays
  // clear of the demo producers' 101–105; Revoke Invite deletes this user, and
  // the code with it, at the end of the folder.
  bru.setVar("inviteSubProducer", String(60 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 39)));
}

body:json {
  {
    "lastName": "Invitee",
    "allstateSubProducerCode": "{{inviteSubProducer}}"
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("stores the sub-producer code zero-padded", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().allstateSubProducerCode).to.equal(
      `0${bru.getVar("inviteSubProducer")}`,
    );
  });

  test("leaves the fields it was not sent alone", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.firstName).to.equal("Pending");
    expect(body.allstateBindId).to.equal(
      bru.getVar("inviteBindId").toUpperCase(),
    );
  });
}

docs {
  # PATCH /users/:userId/details — correct someone's name or Allstate codes (PAC-173)

  **Module** — none (`@SkipModule`). **Permission** — `agency:users:write`
  (Agency Owner). The user must belong to the caller's agency (`404`
  otherwise). Works on active users, pending invites and removed users alike:
  a leaver's Bind ID still names who bound their old sales.

  **Body** — every field `clearable`: a value sets, `null` or `""` clears,
  omitting the key leaves it alone.

  | field | type | rules |
  |---|---|---|
  | firstName | string \| null | trimmed, ≤ 100 |
  | lastName | string \| null | trimmed, ≤ 100 |
  | allstateBindId | string \| null | Allstate portal login; letters, digits, `.` `_` `-`, ≤ 32; stored upper-cased |
  | allstateSubProducerCode | string \| null | ≤ 3 digits, stored zero-padded (`34` → `034`); `000` refused |

  The codes are what Dash Reconciliation credits a producer by, and a Bind ID
  on no user that Dash prints no name for marks a policy as Allstate's own
  1-800 business (a named one reads as a former employee's) — after setting
  one, re-check the month's run (`POST /carrier-reconciliation/runs/:id/reclassify`).

  **Response `200`** — the user, exactly as `GET /users/:userId` returns it
  (codes absent when unset).

  **Errors**
  - `400` — a malformed code, or `000` as a sub-producer code (see
    **Update User Details (000 Sub-producer)**)
  - `403` — caller lacks `agency:users:write`
  - `404` — no such user in this agency
  - `409` `ALLSTATE_CODE_DUPLICATE` — another user holds the code (see
    **Update User Details (Duplicate Code)**)
}
